## Root cause

The MMUAD multi-object metrics synthesized fallback prediction identities from each pandas `DataFrame` index label whenever `output_track_id`/`track_id` was absent or missing.

Index labels are not row identities and do not have to be unique. After concatenation or filtering, two distinct anonymous prediction rows can therefore share an index label and receive the same synthetic track ID. That silently reduces `track_count` and can suppress genuine ID switches. Merely relabeling an otherwise identical estimates table changed the reported MOT metrics.

## Fix

- synthesize anonymous identities from deterministic row positions rather than external index labels;
- keep generated identities distinct from every present user-provided ID;
- install the replacement at both the public compatibility package and its active maintained `_IMPL` boundary;
- register the fix through the repository's core startup-hook mechanism.

## Regression coverage

The focused test compares metrics from identical estimate rows with unique and duplicate pandas index labels. It covers all three public paths:

- no prediction-ID column;
- a missing `track_id` column value; and
- a missing `output_track_id` column value.

For each path, metrics must be index-invariant, report two anonymous tracks, and retain the expected ID switch against one continuing ground-truth object.

## Validation

- isolated patch harness passed all three identity paths, generated-ID collision avoidance, and idempotent installation;
- Python bytecode compilation passed for the patch and focused regression;
- changed Python lines are within the repository's 100-character limit;
- branch is based on current `main` (`8e0431bab0a0b292a46a4ef3ef37051a07c0d4eb`), three commits ahead and zero behind;
- diff is limited to the startup registration, isolated MOT patch, and focused regression test.

GitHub Actions provides the authoritative repository-wide pytest and Ruff validation.

## User outcome

Technical phrases now participate in the same durable learning loop as vocabulary. Ratings survive reload, logout/login and device changes; phrases receive spaced repetition dates, appear in due counts and contribute to retained-learning metrics.

This PR also fixes the reported exercise mismatch: a cloze prompt such as `We need to identify the _____ cause.` now expects the missing English fragment `root`. It no longer checks the Russian translation or displays unrelated Russian phrase choices.

Closes #16.

## Product changes

- add 24 technical phrases to the backend learning catalog;
- enroll phrases for existing and newly registered users;
- store explicit cloze prompts and cloze answers;
- reuse the existing Again / Almost / Known scheduler and review history;
- support persistent and resumable phrase lessons;
- expose full and due phrase catalogs through authenticated APIs;
- show separate word and phrase due/mastered metrics;
- add weekly retained items split into words and phrases;
- replace the phrase exercise contract with English cloze recall;
- retain translation, work example and usage note as corrective feedback;
- keep the previous frontend component in the repository as rollback while activating the new component through `page.tsx`.

## Acceptance criteria

- `We need to identify the _____ cause.` accepts and offers `root`;
- Russian translations are not used as answer choices for English cloze exercises;
- every rated phrase creates one durable review event;
- phrase due date changes immediately after review;
- reviewed phrases disappear from the current due queue;
- phrase progress remains after a new login;
- phrases can be resumed through the existing active lesson endpoint;
- progress reports phrase counts separately and includes retained phrase learning.

## Validation

- frontend unit regression for the root-cause mismatch;
- PostgreSQL + Redis integration test covering registration → due phrase → lesson → review → due queue → login → progress;
- all existing word learning and lesson-resume tests;
- frontend lint, TypeScript, unit tests and production build;
- API/web Docker builds and vulnerability checks.
